@startuml
title Facade / Façade

skinparam legendBackgroundColor #f9f9f9
skinparam legendBorderColor #999999

legend right

**Intent**:
Provide a unified, simpler interface to a subsystem.

**Motivation**:
Reduce complexity; provide an entry point.

**Applicability**:
Reduce learning curve; hide complexity; decouple clients from subsystem.

**Participants**:
Facade delegates to multiple subsystem classes.

**Consequences**:
Pros: Cleaner API; decoupling; easier maintenance.
Cons: Risk of god-object; may hide important features.

**Implementation Notes**:
Keep facade thin; consider multiple facades per context.
Combine with DI to inject subsystems.

**Known Uses**:
Spring’s RestTemplate / WebClient facades over HTTP; Hibernate Session.

**Related Patterns**:
Adapter (change interface), Mediator (coordinate colleagues),
Singleton (single access point).

endlegend

class Facade {
  +operation()
}

class SubsystemA {
  +a1()
}
class SubsystemB {
  +b1()
}
class SubsystemC {
  +c1()
}

Facade ..> SubsystemA
Facade ..> SubsystemB
Facade ..> SubsystemC

class Client
Client ..> Facade
@enduml